  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SF-126 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets SF-126. This indicates a direct, mechanistically linked interaction between Mollicellin N and SF-126, mediated by the intermediate compound 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. The cumulative scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and plausible relationship, though the strength of the evidence varies slightly across the paths. The shared involvement of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a common target reinforces the central role of this compound in the pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Mollicellin N modulates SF-126 through this intermediate, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and functional significance.",
